{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"G23 exact merged-SHA independent review receipt, part 2/3 (29 rows). Nonauthor /root reviewed all 86 Sphalerite blocks at candidate 7d641e07f8303cf97782c6bc1f544b8244cd3f07; all 32 grouped path blobs are byte-identical at merged Gerrit 3094 SHA 255f977212c05404d2a4771ef63435e6dd9febe8. Every row has directives, semantic preservation, and bloat removal PASS. Full TSV SHA-256 de5482cb9f3ae7e496922439c87260d83d6264ef24d27a5be7f57d0c6f777247; chunk SHA-256 900dad50c2c37032441ff84d97c4a3ca75ad91e63f5bc0b007b29d1047491824.\n\n```tsv\nticket\tstable_block_id\tbefore_citation\tfinal_citation\tpreserved_contract_or_consumer\tbefore_words\tafter_words\tdirectives_exact\tsemantic_preservation\tbloat_removal\treviewer_session\nsphalerite-bereft-tortoise\t.github/workflows/_optionality.yml#C:lines-177-183\t10fd0737eb7394804a63d0a779b3676c21296bb0:.github/workflows/_optionality.yml:177-183\t255f977212c05404d2a4771ef63435e6dd9febe8:.github/workflows/_optionality.yml:148-149\t# Run missing-agent degradation tests in a lean venv. The default dev suite # installs agents and skips them. Install only light test dependencies here.\t72\t23\tPASS\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root:2026-10-23\nsphalerite-bereft-tortoise\t.github/workflows/_optionality.yml#C:lines-217-223\t10fd0737eb7394804a63d0a779b3676c21296bb0:.github/workflows/_optionality.yml:217-223\t255f977212c05404d2a4771ef63435e6dd9febe8:.github/workflows/_optionality.yml:183-184\t# Check fail-closed completion when the agents extra is absent in this lean # venv. Offline tests use the shared 300-second thread timeout.\t85\t21\tPASS\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root:2026-10-23\nsphalerite-bereft-tortoise\t.github/workflows/_optionality.yml#C:lines-229-236\t10fd0737eb7394804a63d0a779b3676c21296bb0:.github/workflows/_optionality.yml:229-236\t255f977212c05404d2a4771ef63435e6dd9febe8:.github/workflows/_optionality.yml:190-192\t# Test each extra in its own fresh venv, then test the union. Sequential # iterations save CI slots without allowing one extra's dependencies to # satisfy another's missing declaration.\t106\t27\tPASS\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root:2026-10-23\nsphalerite-bereft-tortoise\t.github/workflows/_optionality.yml#C:lines-333-347\t10fd0737eb7394804a63d0a779b3676c21296bb0:.github/workflows/_optionality.yml:333-347\t255f977212c05404d2a4771ef63435e6dd9febe8:.github/workflows/_optionality.yml:289-292\t# Run every extra through its own absolute venv interpreter. Sourcing env # scripts or calling ambient python can silently retest the first extra. # Each iteration chains commands because bash disables errexit inside if. # Record each failure, continue checking, and return the aggregate status.\t159\t42\tPASS\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root:2026-10-23\nsphalerite-bereft-tortoise\t.github/workflows/_optionality.yml#C:lines-433-441\t10fd0737eb7394804a63d0a779b3676c21296bb0:.github/workflows/_optionality.yml:433-441\t255f977212c05404d2a4771ef63435e6dd9febe8:.github/workflows/_optionality.yml:378-380\t# Verified loads this workflow from main but tests the patchset tree. A patchset # predating the corroborator test must skip before installs, or pytest exits 4 # and casts a false Verified -1. The canary returns when the tree includes it.\t117\t39\tPASS\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root:2026-10-23\nsphalerite-bereft-tortoise\t.github/workflows/codeql.yml#C:lines-3-8\t10fd0737eb7394804a63d0a779b3676c21296bb0:.github/workflows/codeql.yml:3-8\t255f977212c05404d2a4771ef63435e6dd9febe8:.github/workflows/codeql.yml:3-5\t# Scheduled and manual static analysis on the read-only GitHub mirror. # CodeQL writes Security findings without changing the tree. This complements # the Gerrit secret and dependency scans. Actions use the repository's major tags.\t78\t32\tPASS\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root:2026-10-23\nsphalerite-bereft-tortoise\t.github/workflows/codeql.yml#C:lines-10-19\t10fd0737eb7394804a63d0a779b3676c21296bb0:.github/workflows/codeql.yml:10-19\t255f977212c05404d2a4771ef63435e6dd9febe8:.github/workflows/codeql.yml:7-9\t# Scan main on the shared six-hour branch-health schedule. Push-triggered # runs canceled each other, while manual dispatch remains available for an # immediate scan.\t127\t22\tPASS\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root:2026-10-23\nsphalerite-bereft-tortoise\t.github/workflows/codeql.yml#C:lines-22-24\t10fd0737eb7394804a63d0a779b3676c21296bb0:.github/workflows/codeql.yml:22-24\t255f977212c05404d2a4771ef63435e6dd9febe8:.github/workflows/codeql.yml:12-12\t# Stagger at minute 35 from sibling health workflows to reduce queueing.\t32\t11\tPASS\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root:2026-10-23\nsphalerite-bereft-tortoise\t.github/workflows/compact-sweep.yml#C:lines-1-24\t10fd0737eb7394804a63d0a779b3676c21296bb0:.github/workflows/compact-sweep.yml:1-24\t255f977212c05404d2a4771ef63435e6dd9febe8:.github/workflows/compact-sweep.yml:1-5\t# Optional out-of-band ticket compaction on a disposable runner. # Fold tickets above compact.threshold into snapshots and push once. A fresh # full-history clone avoids local writer locks. Concurrent new events merge with # retired-source snapshots as a union. Failed local commits are discarded with # the runner. Six-hour scheduling and single fli\t249\t52\tPASS\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root:2026-10-23\nsphalerite-bereft-tortoise\t.github/workflows/compact-sweep.yml#C:lines-55-59\t10fd0737eb7394804a63d0a779b3676c21296bb0:.github/workflows/compact-sweep.yml:55-59\t255f977212c05404d2a4771ef63435e6dd9febe8:.github/workflows/compact-sweep.yml:36-37\t# Stop the optional sweep after 60 minutes instead of GitHub's six-hour # default. A truncated sweep is harmless because the next run resumes work.\t67\t23\tPASS\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root:2026-10-23\nsphalerite-bereft-tortoise\t.github/workflows/compact-sweep.yml#C:lines-69-73\t10fd0737eb7394804a63d0a779b3676c21296bb0:.github/workflows/compact-sweep.yml:69-73\t255f977212c05404d2a4771ef63435e6dd9febe8:.github/workflows/compact-sweep.yml:47-48\t# Fetch full ticket history. Shallow grafts break merge-base and can resurrect # retired events during compaction. Reconcile by merge, never rebase.\t51\t20\tPASS\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root:2026-10-23\nsphalerite-bereft-tortoise\t.github/workflows/compact-sweep.yml#C:lines-88-91\t10fd0737eb7394804a63d0a779b3676c21296bb0:.github/workflows/compact-sweep.yml:88-91\t255f977212c05404d2a4771ef63435e6dd9febe8:.github/workflows/compact-sweep.yml:63-64\t# Mount the writable store on the tickets branch so tracker.branch matches # and store fsck does not report a detached or mismatched checkout.\t53\t23\tPASS\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root:2026-10-23\nsphalerite-bereft-tortoise\t.github/workflows/compact-sweep.yml#C:lines-104-107\t10fd0737eb7394804a63d0a779b3676c21296bb0:.github/workflows/compact-sweep.yml:104-107\t255f977212c05404d2a4771ef63435e6dd9febe8:.github/workflows/compact-sweep.yml:77-78\t# Set Git identity for both the checkout and mounted ticket worktree. # The bot email also resolves the optional snapshot signing identity.\t48\t21\tPASS\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root:2026-10-23\nsphalerite-bereft-tortoise\t.github/workflows/compact-sweep.yml#C:lines-117-122\t10fd0737eb7394804a63d0a779b3676c21296bb0:.github/workflows/compact-sweep.yml:117-122\t255f977212c05404d2a4771ef63435e6dd9febe8:.github/workflows/compact-sweep.yml:88-89\t# Materialize an optional signing key in a 0600 runner-temp file. Without it, # snapshots remain unsigned. The mounted store carries its own .env-id.\t67\t22\tPASS\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root:2026-10-23\nsphalerite-bereft-tortoise\t.github/workflows/compact-sweep.yml#C:lines-147-152\t10fd0737eb7394804a63d0a779b3676c21296bb0:.github/workflows/compact-sweep.yml:147-152\t255f977212c05404d2a4771ef63435e6dd9febe8:.github/workflows/compact-sweep.yml:114-115\t# Exit 2 reports partial sweep errors as a warning. Exit 1 fails the job. # Capture output without a pipe so a tee failure cannot hide rebar's exit code.\t60\t28\tPASS\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root:2026-10-23\nsphalerite-bereft-tortoise\t.github/workflows/compact-sweep.yml#C:lines-162-165\t10fd0737eb7394804a63d0a779b3676c21296bb0:.github/workflows/compact-sweep.yml:162-165\t255f977212c05404d2a4771ef63435e6dd9febe8:.github/workflows/compact-sweep.yml:125-125\t# Publish fold counts every run so stalled or empty sweeps are visible.\t53\t12\tPASS\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root:2026-10-23\nsphalerite-bereft-tortoise\t.github/workflows/dependency-advisory-canary.yml#C:lines-1-25\t10fd0737eb7394804a63d0a779b3676c21296bb0:.github/workflows/dependency-advisory-canary.yml:1-25\t255f977212c05404d2a4771ef63435e6dd9febe8:.github/workflows/dependency-advisory-canary.yml:1-5\t# Daily advisory check for the committed uv.lock dependency closure. # Critical or high findings keep one tagged bug current, with at most one # comment per 24 hours. Clearing findings closes it. Release authorization # blocks on advisory findings, while ordinary Gerrit changes remain reviewable. # scripts/dependency_audit.py owns classification an\t247\t51\tPASS\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root:2026-10-23\nsphalerite-bereft-tortoise\t.github/workflows/dependency-advisory-canary.yml#C:lines-131-140\t10fd0737eb7394804a63d0a779b3676c21296bb0:.github/workflows/dependency-advisory-canary.yml:131-140\t255f977212c05404d2a4771ef63435e6dd9febe8:.github/workflows/dependency-advisory-canary.yml:111-113\t# Keep audit continue-on-error so the alert step still runs on findings. # A crashed audit leaves blocking output empty. The alert step rejects that # state and fails the run. Do not allow the alert step to continue on error.\t105\t38\tPASS\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root:2026-10-23\nsphalerite-bereft-tortoise\t.github/workflows/external-integration.yml#C:lines-3-34\t10fd0737eb7394804a63d0a779b3676c21296bb0:.github/workflows/external-integration.yml:3-34\t255f977212c05404d2a4771ef63435e6dd9febe8:.github/workflows/external-integration.yml:3-7\t# Manual and scheduled integration checks against billable or external services. # Provider-isolated LLM arms require their own credentials and record usage. # Separate jobs cover non-LLM services, temporary Langfuse, Jira Data Center, # Jira Cloud with S3, and Linux/macOS Pandoc corpus replay. These jobs stay # outside the automatic test gate. Mis\t275\t54\tPASS\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root:2026-10-23\nsphalerite-bereft-tortoise\t.github/workflows/external-integration.yml#C:lines-161-168\t10fd0737eb7394804a63d0a779b3676c21296bb0:.github/workflows/external-integration.yml:161-168\t255f977212c05404d2a4771ef63435e6dd9febe8:.github/workflows/external-integration.yml:134-136\t# GitHub runners lack the review bot's EC2 instance role and IMDS route. # This arm uses a repository-scoped OIDC role limited to Anthropic Bedrock # invocation instead of a stored AWS access key.\t96\t31\tPASS\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root:2026-10-23\nsphalerite-bereft-tortoise\t.github/workflows/external-integration.yml#C:lines-199-216\t10fd0737eb7394804a63d0a779b3676c21296bb0:.github/workflows/external-integration.yml:199-216\t255f977212c05404d2a4771ef63435e6dd9febe8:.github/workflows/external-integration.yml:167-170\t# Set both AWS_DEFAULT_REGION and REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION on every arm. # IMDS supplies no region here, and tests may select Bedrock across provider # arms. Rebar's variable also records provider provenance. The repository # variable falls back to us-east-1. Missing resolution raises LLMConfigError.\t181\t38\tPASS\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root:2026-10-23\nsphalerite-bereft-tortoise\t.github/workflows/external-integration.yml#C:lines-227-241\t10fd0737eb7394804a63d0a779b3676c21296bb0:.github/workflows/external-integration.yml:227-241\t255f977212c05404d2a4771ef63435e6dd9febe8:.github/workflows/external-integration.yml:181-183\t# Select modules marked llm_live once per provider. The other external # job runs the complement, and new marked modules join automatically. # A 900-second thread watchdog names blocked calls before GitHub's job limit.\t189\t31\tPASS\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root:2026-10-23\nsphalerite-bereft-tortoise\t.github/workflows/external-integration.yml#C:lines-375-401\t10fd0737eb7394804a63d0a779b3676c21296bb0:.github/workflows/external-integration.yml:375-401\t255f977212c05404d2a4771ef63435e6dd9febe8:.github/workflows/external-integration.yml:317-320\t# Isolate temp and cache state. Exclude Data Center and S3 rehearsal suites # from this Cloud job so its all-skip canary cannot mask their skipped tests. # Exclude provider-matrix LLM modules to avoid duplicate billing and masking # skipped Jira tests. A 600-second thread watchdog bounds each test.\t324\t45\tPASS\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root:2026-10-23\nsphalerite-bereft-tortoise\t.github/workflows/external-integration.yml#C:lines-478-485\t10fd0737eb7394804a63d0a779b3676c21296bb0:.github/workflows/external-integration.yml:478-485\t255f977212c05404d2a4771ef63435e6dd9febe8:.github/workflows/external-integration.yml:397-399\t# Server health can precede database migrations. Probe the public REST API # with headless-init credentials until the project resolves. Keep probe # errors visible instead of reporting them as a readiness timeout.\t80\t30\tPASS\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root:2026-10-23\nsphalerite-bereft-tortoise\t.github/workflows/external-integration.yml#C:lines-542-552\t10fd0737eb7394804a63d0a779b3676c21296bb0:.github/workflows/external-integration.yml:542-552\t255f977212c05404d2a4771ef63435e6dd9febe8:.github/workflows/external-integration.yml:456-458\t# Install jira-datacenter for the transport dependency. Smoke tests alone # can pass while every transport test skips, so the transport suite fails # explicitly if its dependency is absent after harness readiness.\t109\t30\tPASS\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root:2026-10-23\nsphalerite-bereft-tortoise\t.github/workflows/external-integration.yml#C:lines-588-637\t10fd0737eb7394804a63d0a779b3676c21296bb0:.github/workflows/external-integration.yml:588-637\t255f977212c05404d2a4771ef63435e6dd9febe8:.github/workflows/external-integration.yml:494-501\t# -rA exposes captured output from passing Data Center tests, including # measured responses and field-readiness timing. Epic fields register after # the first Software project is created. If they remain absent, inspect the # field inventory before changing the readiness timeout. # The 900-second per-test thread guard covers documented readiness wa\t591\t79\tPASS\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root:2026-10-23\nsphalerite-bereft-tortoise\t.github/workflows/external-integration.yml#C:lines-651-664\t10fd0737eb7394804a63d0a779b3676c21296bb0:.github/workflows/external-integration.yml:651-664\t255f977212c05404d2a4771ef63435e6dd9febe8:.github/workflows/external-integration.yml:515-517\t# Read-only many-to-many rehearsal against REB and DIG on an isolated S3 # store. Run only when the scoped S3 OIDC role is configured. The Bedrock # role grants no S3 access. Jira counts and a structural guard detect writes.\t152\t37\tPASS\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root:2026-10-23\nsphalerite-bereft-tortoise\t.github/workflows/external-integration.yml#C:lines-797-812\t10fd0737eb7394804a63d0a779b3676c21296bb0:.github/workflows/external-integration.yml:797-812\t255f977212c05404d2a4771ef63435e6dd9febe8:.github/workflows/external-integration.yml:650-653\t# Exercise coordinator create, binding, commit-unknown, and fuse paths in # Jira Cloud. Restrict writes to one issue with a unique run label. The test # cleans it in finally, and an always-run step repeats cleanup on failure. # The all-skip canary prevents a skipped lane from reporting green.\t150\t45\tPASS\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root:2026-10-23\nsphalerite-bereft-tortoise\t.github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml#C:lines-3-21\t10fd0737eb7394804a63d0a779b3676c21296bb0:.github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml:3-21\t255f977212c05404d2a4771ef63435e6dd9febe8:.github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml:3-7\t# Gerrit Verified vote for an exact patchset, dispatched on patchset creation or # recheck. Clear the old vote, run the shared gates, then cast +1 or -1 with the # run URL. Trusted default-branch vote code and the SSH key stay outside patchset # execution. Missing required repository variables or key fails closed. # Third-party actions retain their\t155\t57\tPASS\tPASS\tPASS\tagent:/root:2026-10-23\n```"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1792818220647942750,"uuid":"fdb6e681-32f0-472a-bab6-3ab1562ca4fc"}